<title>NORWAY: FORECAST - Dyno Q1 profits seen rising.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dyno Q1 profits seen rising.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian chemicals group Dyno Industrier ASA is expected to post first-quarter pre-tax profits of 101 million crowns, up from 86 million in the same year-ago period, according to eight analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>Two analysts suggested to buy the share, three said hold and two said sell. One declined to make a recommendation.</p>
<p>Most believed that Dyno has achieved higher methanol prices so far this year compared to the first quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>The big question for Dyno is its restructuring plans which will be presented with the first-quarter results on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;If you believe in these plans you have every reason to be optimistic,&quot; one analyst said.</p>
<p>Another said: &quot;A shakeup in management might produce a more active organisation, but the company must first prove what it can do before I start believing it.&quot;</p>
